#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054365 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054641 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93bc0caa-2352-5d02-9ccf-7267dff4be2c" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Compound Statements in Symbolic Form"}] :question/id #uuid "a8c9f90f-3c97-5a01-99b5-9a9f8b3eef66" :question/math-academy-id "e-12677" :question/problem "Consider the following statement:\n\n$14$ is divisible by $4$ **or** $\\sqrt{3}$ is a rational number.\n\nWrite this statement in symbolic form using the following notations:\n\n- ![](images/64/64c5006a1d5f6b515ebfb603e5da3d10b44616960afd0dbbcabb32a5a23aed26.svg)\n\n- ![](images/b2/b2d623c77373a42771d812e0242d4545884a79107c1e97769d0f4bb8bb7a7a06.svg)" :question/worked-solution "The word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\lor$\".\n\nSo, the sentence reads\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{14 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is divisible by }\\vphantom{p} 4 }_S \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{or}}_{\\lor} \\quad \\underbrace{\\sqrt{3} \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is a rational number} }_T,\n$$\n\nthat is, $S \\lor T.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054366 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054642 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e2ea816-3a62-5167-9f08-17ebcf97c22e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Nested Compound Statements in Symbolic Form"}] :question/id #uuid "e5a60113-14a0-5468-93b1-7f0eaa6e9a90" :question/math-academy-id "e-12678" :question/problem "$7$ is odd **or** a multiple of $3$, **and** $3$ is less than $7$.\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- ![](images/c9/c99c7535c3d2d6c854aea2e3408d15f2c0ff6423c4010ad211dbb6d576fe6928.svg)\n\n- ![](images/3f/3fca3aace2f71ead6ca860e93e9138abb40559e0eb9434ca068b563380b12912.svg)\n\n- ![](images/76/768f38af5ffc9fc48817db2f054dc9da251a26469a644c0e7eb7141fef54284b.svg)" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\land$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\lor$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $7$ is odd or a multiple of $3.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{7 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is odd }}_P \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{or}}_{\\lor} \\quad \\underbrace{7 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is a multiple of }3}_Q,\n$$\n\nthat is, $P \\lor Q.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $3$ is less than $7$. This corresponds to $R.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{7 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is odd} \\textbf{ or } \\vphantom{p} \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ a multiple of } 3}_{P \\, \\lor \\,Q}, \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{and}}_{\\land} \\quad \n\\underbrace{3 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is less than } 7 }_R\n$$\n\nthat is, $(P \\lor Q) \\land R.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054368 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054643 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "49ab93ca-16ca-5e57-835f-036b59f25d63" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Values of Compound Statements"}] :question/id #uuid "6497cb54-2453-5dd7-8b97-09e06280d774" :question/math-academy-id "e-12693" :question/problem "Consider the following compound statement:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{5 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is prime} }_A \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{or}}_{\\lor} \\quad \\underbrace{\\dfrac13 \\in \\mathbb{Z}}_B\n$$\n\nFind the truth values of the statements $A$ and $B,$ and the compound statement $A\\lor B.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(\\land)$ and \"or\" $(\\lor)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A \\land B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A \\lor B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $A$ is true, and $B$ is false. Therefore, the result is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{5\\text{ is prime}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{\\frac{1}{3}\\in Z}_{⏟}}_{B} & \\,\\,≡\\,\\text{true}∨\\text{false}≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054389 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054644 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c15e521-f848-5d9c-ba06-00550277b8cb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Values of Complex Statements"}] :question/id #uuid "9209c4e5-30e0-5933-9c41-32750b5301ad" :question/math-academy-id "e-12895" :question/problem "Consider the following compound statement:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\mathbb{Z}\\cup \\mathbb{R}=\\mathbb{Z} }_P \n\\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{|}\\textbf{and}}_{\\land} \\quad \\underbrace{\\overbrace{7 \\,|\\, 21}^Q \n\\quad \\overbrace{\\vphantom{|}\\textbf{or}}^{\\lor} \\quad \n\\overbrace{7 \\,|\\, 29}^R }_{Q \\, \\lor \\, R}\n$$\n\nFind the truth values of the statements $P,$ $Q$ and $R,$ and the compound statements $Q\\lor R$ and $P\\land (Q\\lor R).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(\\land)$ and \"or\" $(\\lor)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A \\land B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A \\lor B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $P$ is false, $Q$ is true, and $R$ is false. Therefore, $Q \\lor R$ is true, but the result is false:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P∧(Q∨R) & ≡\\text{false}∧\\overset{\\text{true}}{\\overset{⏞}{(\\text{true}∨\\text{false})}} \\\\  & ≡\\text{false}∧\\text{true} \\\\  & ≡\\text{false}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496234 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054641 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93bc0caa-2352-5d02-9ccf-7267dff4be2c" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Compound Statements in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac8831f6-0b30-5fff-99a5-bdc86ee2c9df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨(P∧Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495896} {:answer/id #uuid "c788bb6a-3103-557c-8827-e479bc17cfa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495947} {:answer/id #uuid "d65dc866-fd3f-54f7-a7c4-b6f364caf884" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495979} {:answer/id #uuid "edef6b4f-6fa8-5244-a412-5dda014bbd8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧P" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496032} {:answer/id #uuid "fd3b589e-c610-5002-a7df-286e992e76fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧(P∨Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496069}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c788bb6a-3103-557c-8827-e479bc17cfa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495947} :answer-field/id #uuid "fda58e98-bdbc-530e-bf08-2b35adcab71d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496219}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "20409d3d-4f9a-55b3-ae07-39d336721810" :question/math-academy-id "q-170736" :question/problem "Express the statement \"$8$ is a natural number and divisible by $4$\" in symbolic form, where $P=$ \"$8$ is a natural number\" and $Q=$ \"$8$ is divisible by $4.$\"" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧.$\"\n\nNote that the given sentence is a shortened version of the following full sentence:\n\n$8$ is a natural number and $8$ is divisible by $4.$\n\nSo, the sentence reads\n\n$$\n{{8\\text{ is a natural number}}_{⏟}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{8\\text{ is divisible by }4}_{⏟}}_{Q},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∧Q.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389663 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054641 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93bc0caa-2352-5d02-9ccf-7267dff4be2c" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Compound Statements in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58f0507d-20d4-5775-b373-d900d8b96779" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X∧(X∨Y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389665} {:answer/id #uuid "74edb7a8-7861-5d22-ad52-5bf2049659b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y∧Y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389666} {:answer/id #uuid "79bde983-110b-51ba-9196-948da1351529" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X∨Y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389667} {:answer/id #uuid "98ad621e-6a51-525b-87d3-68cb43e74fed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X∧Y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389668} {:answer/id #uuid "9a7c8e26-e02a-5580-a252-6eeef8520438" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X∨(X∧Y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98ad621e-6a51-525b-87d3-68cb43e74fed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X∧Y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389668} :answer-field/id #uuid "40a5c6cf-be89-504a-bea5-37363120d54a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389664}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0c84caa5-0818-5b64-a106-3aa76c7b323f" :question/math-academy-id "q-170738" :question/problem "Express the statement \"$4$ is even and positive\" in symbolic form, where $X=$ \"$4$ is even\" and $Y=$ \"$4$ is positive.\"" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧.$\"\n\nNote that the given sentence is a shortened version of the following full sentence:\n\n$4$ is even and $4$ is positive.\n\nSo, the sentence reads\n\n$$\n{{4\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{X}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{4\\text{ is positive}}_{⏟}}_{Y},\n$$\n\nthat is, $X∧Y.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496313 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054641 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93bc0caa-2352-5d02-9ccf-7267dff4be2c" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Compound Statements in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88911721-9caf-5241-b5ba-5af57e949852" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495805} {:answer/id #uuid "901c3b3b-9f68-5e41-9761-d7d73ac85dfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∧" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495827} {:answer/id #uuid "dd760021-393c-59e1-b51e-32da763bff33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∨" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88911721-9caf-5241-b5ba-5af57e949852" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495805} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c15a5ea-6fbb-5554-b167-3feb951f48f5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496093} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e748ae9-9a3f-5614-b6bc-f2ee460795e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495576} {:answer/id #uuid "767dfd7f-44cf-5e87-a8e7-1723c4a3b904" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495768} {:answer/id #uuid "981d9922-dfe2-5e58-aa67-7e6408d44da9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∨" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495851} {:answer/id #uuid "a118e1cd-a7ba-52a2-85f6-a5b525ec34fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∧" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495869}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "767dfd7f-44cf-5e87-a8e7-1723c4a3b904" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495768} :answer-field/id #uuid "65e86f13-cfaa-54d2-a88c-7dbfbad93e7b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496130} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ba18c82-4fca-5d74-9c39-649a58246820" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495606} {:answer/id #uuid "b9c2b74e-f283-5621-823f-7ea07e5f1f6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495924} {:answer/id #uuid "c13b8279-5235-52d4-8183-9eead02e882a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∨" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495934} {:answer/id #uuid "e8cb8efd-9eb2-5007-a571-6411296a27e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∧" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496024}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8cb8efd-9eb2-5007-a571-6411296a27e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∧" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496024} :answer-field/id #uuid "d713043e-a84c-5e43-8ac1-2406fa552b95" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496190}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d207a2f4-0aa5-5660-b685-cd64ab113d8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-175527" :question/problem "$2$ is odd **and** $3$ is prime.\n\nConsider the compound statement above and the following notations:\n\n- $P:2\\text{ is odd}$\n\n- $Q:3\\text{ is prime}$\n\nExpressed in symbolic form, our statement can be written as\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\".\n\nSo, the sentence reads\n\n$$\n{{2\\text{ is odd}}_{⏟}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{3\\text{ is prime}}_{⏟}}_{Q},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∧Q.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496309 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054643 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "49ab93ca-16ca-5e57-835f-036b59f25d63" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Values of Compound Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "437c25a0-ffe2-5cb2-ab86-2abe4f8570ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495664} {:answer/id #uuid "835af782-c34f-5315-831c-d2d73ce3599a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495792}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "437c25a0-ffe2-5cb2-ab86-2abe4f8570ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495664} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c291b0e-f8c9-5939-a96e-0401075ed43c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496120} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0363b271-e803-5571-b53d-239e604590f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495519} {:answer/id #uuid "cc4cb860-21b2-51d4-b70c-b8f24038b22b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495953}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0363b271-e803-5571-b53d-239e604590f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495519} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5302458-71fb-5afb-a950-a7024e57aebf" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496156} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ea973ca-4c0d-5900-a76d-4213928289f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495618} {:answer/id #uuid "374c1b92-a065-5d73-84bd-e768c04e2423" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "374c1b92-a065-5d73-84bd-e768c04e2423" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495639} :answer-field/id #uuid "c45c4194-12b2-5fe5-9c77-c08f6af56cd8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496174}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c586014f-8b0b-5087-a740-57029ea9f0d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-175666" :question/problem "$$\n{{5\\text{ is odd}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{-5\\in Z}_{⏟}}_{B}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $A$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $B$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $A∨B$ is {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $A$ is true, and $B$ is true. Therefore, the result is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{5\\text{ is odd}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{-5\\in Z}_{⏟}}_{B} & \\,\\,≡\\,\\text{true}∨\\text{true}≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379015 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054643 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "49ab93ca-16ca-5e57-835f-036b59f25d63" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Values of Compound Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df22f795-a009-5641-a379-443361928638" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379017} {:answer/id #uuid "de633a70-3263-5034-98fb-d53bce172bf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379018}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de633a70-3263-5034-98fb-d53bce172bf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379018} :answer-field/id #uuid "d51318db-0570-5f7c-be3d-fcaf41b4d016" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379016} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23d7849b-e56c-547e-bb92-1d1d1d8df933" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379020} {:answer/id #uuid "cbb0cbad-92da-5755-8a8a-ee3831707436" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379021}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23d7849b-e56c-547e-bb92-1d1d1d8df933" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379020} :answer-field/id #uuid "e423f89e-f2a2-5170-a1c1-7dc0a236ee95" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379019} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b435872b-9826-56f1-933c-ff7