/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(A∨B)∧C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495788} {:answer/id #uuid "8aadeebf-6b08-5f6a-a8b4-fccd85c8a92d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∧(B∨C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495814} {:answer/id #uuid "bb1e4737-f068-5dc9-93f9-8719f933ff8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(A∧B)∨C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495925}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb1e4737-f068-5dc9-93f9-8719f933ff8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(A∧B)∨C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495925} :answer-field/id #uuid "c26531b6-83b5-5a81-9950-dbbf13c02146" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496170}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2491e070-37d1-586f-b67e-4103f90ed72e" :question/math-academy-id "q-177454" :question/problem "$7$ is a composite number **and** odd, **or** $2+6\\ge 10.$\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $A:7\\text{ is a composite number}$\n\n- $B:7\\text{ is odd}$\n\n- $C:2+6\\ge 10$" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $7$ is a composite number and odd. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{7\\text{ is a composite number}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{7\\text{ is odd}}_{⏟}}_{B},\n$$\n\nthat is, $A∧B.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $2+6\\ge 10.$ This corresponds to $C.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{7\\text{ is a composite number}\\text{ and }\\text{odd}}_{⏟}}_{A\\,∧\\,B},\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{2+6\\ge 10}_{⏟}}_{C}\n$$\n\nthat is, $(A∧B)∨C.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496272 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054642 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e2ea816-3a62-5167-9f08-17ebcf97c22e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Nested Compound Statements in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "032dbb2a-5dc1-5e48-9134-272eda68f2b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∨(N∧P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495518} {:answer/id #uuid "0476cbd2-78dc-5e1a-9e60-a8bbb1d9dfd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(M∧N)∨P" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495522} {:answer/id #uuid "88b17ea2-775b-5a6a-bd44-82b302f7402b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∧(N∧P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495806} {:answer/id #uuid "8d513d5e-04ef-5ac2-8463-b15a460491d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(M∨N)∧P" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495819} {:answer/id #uuid "8ed61285-624c-56ae-a424-83a7b63683eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(M∨N)∨P" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495824}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d513d5e-04ef-5ac2-8463-b15a460491d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(M∨N)∧P" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495819} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e7284d0-752d-528a-b20a-055a37d2c544" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496101}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "717ad532-4709-5a63-b627-09752527f241" :question/math-academy-id "q-177457" :question/problem "$4$ is even **or** ${4}^{2}=12$, **and** $-2$ is an integer number.\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $M:4\\text{ is even}$\n\n- $N:{4}^{2}=12$\n\n- $P:-2\\text{ is an integer number}$" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $4$ is even or ${4}^{2}=12.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{4\\text{ is even }}_{⏟}}_{M}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{{4}^{2}=12}_{⏟}}_{N},\n$$\n\nthat is, $M∨N.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $-2$ is an integer number. This corresponds to $P.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{4\\text{ is even}\\text{ or }{4}^{2}=12}_{⏟}}_{M\\,∨\\,N},\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{-2\\text{ is an integer number}}_{⏟}}_{P}\n$$\n\nthat is, $(M∨N)∧P.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496275 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054642 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e2ea816-3a62-5167-9f08-17ebcf97c22e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Nested Compound Statements in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08226b09-094d-55bc-a500-13e7bd894d3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(M∧P)∨(N∧Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495532} {:answer/id #uuid "62d1f44f-6042-5734-9027-0993b4819b69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(M∨P)∨(N∧Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495731} {:answer/id #uuid "68da953e-294d-510b-94be-5d9e6008ed59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(M∨P)∨(N∨Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495743} {:answer/id #uuid "cdd60e3e-cf9b-5874-8cb9-65b6ab83f9ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(M∧P)∧(N∧Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495957} {:answer/id #uuid "d2f3e577-3286-59cc-928d-270004a2410d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(M∧N)∧(P∧Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495973}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08226b09-094d-55bc-a500-13e7bd894d3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(M∧P)∨(N∧Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495532} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae713bc7-7c15-5579-a80d-6099f958e0e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496160}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7d328347-cdbe-5da0-b048-5a26fc979b28" :question/math-academy-id "q-177717" :question/problem "$6|10$ **and** $6|18,$ **or** $11$ is prime **and** odd.\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $M:6|10$\n\n- $P:6|18$\n\n- $N:11\\text{ is prime}$\n\n- $Q:11\\text{ is odd}$" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $6|10$ and $6|18.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{6|10}_{⏟}}_{M}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{6|18}_{⏟}}_{P}\n$$\n\nthat is, $M∧P.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $11$ is prime and odd. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{11\\text{ is prime}}_{⏟}}_{N}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{11\\text{ is odd }}_{⏟}}_{Q},\n$$\n\nthat is, $N∧Q.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{6|10\\text{ and }6|18}_{⏟}}_{M\\,∧\\,P}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{11\\text{ is prime }\\text{and}\\text{ odd }}_{⏟}}_{N\\,∧\\,Q},\n$$\n\nthat is, $(M∧P)∨(N∧Q).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389825 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054644 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c15e521-f848-5d9c-ba06-00550277b8cb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Values of Complex Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "562c9283-48db-53e3-8e1b-90f287599846" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389827} {:answer/id #uuid "ad7fa272-b6f8-590f-9c5b-65d9f9dfa430" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389828}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad7fa272-b6f8-590f-9c5b-65d9f9dfa430" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389828} :answer-field/id #uuid "48a24199-8fbc-5f8a-be94-b1433383cd8d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389826} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff4660a1-9de3-5baa-87b3-1593351fefd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389830} {:answer/id #uuid "23d43ed5-1f81-5a25-b0c9-296027e1069f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff4660a1-9de3-5baa-87b3-1593351fefd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389830} :answer-field/id #uuid "8252abad-b399-5caf-b293-dc6a3db02c60" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389829} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf7d3285-15e0-5c92-91fa-76404ef88ea4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389833} {:answer/id #uuid "5bb36f52-020a-5e2f-84e1-9b8fce7b0301" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389834}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf7d3285-15e0-5c92-91fa-76404ef88ea4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389833} :answer-field/id #uuid "790a635b-b899-57d8-88e4-a24e66556c49" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389832}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fb4c15c3-7ea2-5717-b42a-a17f62554b99" :question/math-academy-id "q-178151" :question/problem "$$\n{{N\\cap Z=N}_{⏟}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{3\\text{ is even}}}\\,\\overset{∨}{\\overset{⏞}{\\text{or}}}\\,\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{39\\text{ is prime}}}}_{⏟}}_{Q\\,∨\\,R}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $P$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $Q∨R$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $P∧(Q∨R)$ is {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $P$ is true, $Q$ is false, and $R$ is false. Therefore, $Q∨R$ is false, and the result is false:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P∧(Q∨R) & ≡\\text{true}∧\\overset{\\text{false}}{\\overset{⏞}{(\\text{false}∨\\text{false})}} \\\\  & ≡\\text{true}∧\\text{false} \\\\  & ≡\\text{false}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055061 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054644 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c15e521-f848-5d9c-ba06-00550277b8cb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Values of Complex Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89ac148b-88b6-5bc6-a50e-f6603a28bd8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051860} {:answer/id #uuid "c9897358-adb8-5e1a-abf0-2d661694ad76" :answer/type {:db/id #e