81}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5f1de2e0-3e98-599c-9d88-57f6ce468e91" :question/math-academy-id "q-178160" :question/problem "$$\n{{\\{1,2\\}\\cup \\{3\\}=\\{1,2,3\\}}_{⏟}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{0\\in Z}}\\,\\overset{∧}{\\overset{⏞}{\\text{and}}}\\,\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{1\\text{ is positive}}}}_{⏟}}_{Q\\,∧\\,R}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $P$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $Q∧R$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $P∧(Q∧R)$ is {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $P$ is true, $Q$ is true, and $R$ is true. Therefore, $Q∧R$ is true, and the result is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P∧(Q∧R) & ≡\\text{true}∧\\overset{\\text{true}}{\\overset{⏞}{(\\text{true}∧\\text{true})}} \\\\  & ≡\\text{true}∧\\text{true} \\\\  & ≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496324 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054644 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c15e521-f848-5d9c-ba06-00550277b8cb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Values of Complex Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2046c2fd-a8d4-54d2-8ffd-95ecd612b6eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495578} {:answer/id #uuid "46b2322d-6809-5d8b-883d-878f30de914e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495671}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2046c2fd-a8d4-54d2-8ffd-95ecd612b6eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495578} :answer-field/id #uuid "62493ac5-f15b-51cb-8a00-6c91b7e0c5cd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496125} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d0928b9-6aee-5a24-8532-dfa31a856083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495569} {:answer/id #uuid "f9d30708-c054-535c-8d52-04c500ecca7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496056}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d0928b9-6aee-5a24-8532-dfa31a856083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495569} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf4f5979-2231-543e-a839-0854443bf580" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496169} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5fd4d05-59ac-59bc-a081-aec213d99bba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495883} {:answer/id #uuid "fa0877b1-0fd1-5c32-9fec-6b40f84addfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496058}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa0877b1-0fd1-5c32-9fec-6b40f84addfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496058} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9feaa5e-9db9-5e7e-a63b-25953d48d1fe" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496179}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e7eb8fb9-95e2-5b65-af61-0f6fe58c75b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-178162" :question/problem "$$\n{{\\overset{P}{\\overset{⏞}{0\\le -1}}\\,\\overset{∨}{\\overset{⏞}{\\text{or}}}\\,\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{3\\,|\\,7}}}_{⏟}}_{P\\,∨\\,Q}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{14\\text{ is prime}}_{⏟}}_{R}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $P∨Q$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $R$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $(P∨Q)∨R$ is {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $P$ is false, $Q$ is false, and $R$ is false. Therefore, $P∨Q$ is false, and the result is false:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(P∨Q)∨R & ≡\\overset{\\text{false}}{\\overset{⏞}{(\\text{false}∨\\text{false})}}∨\\text{false} \\\\  & ≡\\text{false}∨\\text{false} \\\\  & ≡\\text{false}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496270 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054642 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e2ea816-3a62-5167-9f08-17ebcf97c22e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Nested Compound Statements in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74a9345e-0af6-509c-8b78-a9538e02cac1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R∨(P∧R)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495764} {:answer/id #uuid "d5e0c017-0650-5764-b19c-c2f60dd1e1d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨(Q∨R)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495978} {:answer/id #uuid "df90fb44-f536-52ae-af21-87646c000413" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨(Q∧R)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496005} {:answer/id #uuid "fa14aaed-5c59-5d07-b8f0-fe4765c03035" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧(Q∧R)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496059} {:answer/id #uuid "fcd84110-304d-56fc-9282-893719df54f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R∧(P∨Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496068}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d5e0c017-0650-5764-b19c-c2f60dd1e1d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨(Q∨R)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495978} :answer-field/id #uuid "99a22f08-f710-5288-add1-9afdd22d06f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496150}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6a09aec4-5239-540b-baf9-5ce099cfcf55" :question/math-academy-id "q-178520" :question/problem "$9$ is a perfect square, **or** $3\\ge 4$ **or** $3=5-1.$\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $P:9\\text{ is a perfect square}$\n\n- $Q:3\\ge 4$\n\n- $R:3=5-1$" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $9$ is a perfect square. This corresponds to $P.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $3\\ge 4$ or $3=5-1.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{3\\ge 4}_{⏟}}_{Q}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{3=5-1}_{⏟}}_{R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $Q∨R.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{9\\text{ is a perfect square}}_{⏟}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{3\\ge 4\\text{ or }3=5-1}_{⏟}}_{Q\\,∨\\,R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∨(Q∨R).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496223 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054642 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e2ea816-3a62-5167-9f08-17ebcf97c22e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Nested Compound Statements in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cb8259e-2609-557c-a939-ddc327a5eee5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(P∨R)∧Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495610} {:answer/id #uuid "5c299c17-f506-596c-90eb-cd4f3d6b42a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(R∧P)∨Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495720} {:answer/id #uuid "8a379917-531a-54d8-af3e-0292be053dd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(P∧Q)∨R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495812} {:answer/id #uuid "a5d7f2f3-23a8-5dc8-a56c-57b04c083e5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(P∧Q)∧R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495882} {:answer/id #uuid "d75f9393-172b-5f63-857d-7b40f1ba5376" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(P∨Q)∨R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495985}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5d7f2f3-23a8-5dc8-a56c-57b04c083e5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(P∧Q)∧R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495882} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e4e5ae8-a2a5-5b36-a2dc-8b979138fc73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496122}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "02eac488-c624-58c9-8e5f-2f3e12e226ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-178524" :question/problem "$6\\le {3}^{2}$ **and** $6$ is even, **and** $13$ is a prime number.\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $P:6\\le {3}^{2}$\n\n- $Q:6\\text{ is even}$\n\n- $R:13\\text{ is a prime number}$" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $6\\le {3}^{2}$ and $6$ is even. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{6\\le {3}^{2}}_{⏟}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{6\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{Q},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∧Q.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $13$ is a prime number. This corresponds to $R.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{6\\le {3}^{2}\\text{ and }6\\text{ is even }}_{⏟}}_{P\\,∧\\,Q},\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{13\\text{ is a prime number}}_{⏟}}_{R}\n$$\n\nthat is, $(P∧Q)∧R.$"}]}
